From d6906b476bf5968bb69c06366dd0b8b5f0d93da8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AOSP RK3576 Baseline <uhf-platform@localbuild>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 10:31:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 09/17] uhf: wire services.core.unboosted to the
 rockchip.uhf.aidl Java library

Real build failure, found by actually running the build (not by
inspection):

  frameworks/base/services/core/java/com/android/server/uhf/UhfHalTransport.java:25:
  error: symbol not found rockchip.uhf.aidl.IUhfReader

UhfHalTransport.java has imported rockchip.uhf.aidl.IUhfReader since the
Phase 2 HAL-transport commit, but services/core/Android.bp's
services.core.unboosted module was never given a static_libs dependency
on the generated AIDL Java library, so it only ever compiled by accident
in prior manual/partial verification passes that didn't build this
target - the first time the real services.core.unboosted module actually
got compiled (via make update-api's system-server-stubs dependency
chain) this surfaced immediately.

Fix: add "rockchip.uhf.aidl-java" next to this file's other AIDL/HIDL HAL
Java libraries (android.hardware.boot-V1-java, android.hardware.health-V2-java,
etc.) in static_libs. Confirmed the exact generated module name against
system/tools/aidl/build/aidl_interface.go:378 ("When enabled, this
creates a target called '<name>-java'.") rather than guessing - our
aidl_interface has no versions_with_info (see the two prior commits in
this series fixing that), so it's the unversioned "<name>-java" form, not
a "-V1-java" suffix.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 services/core/Android.bp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/services/core/Android.bp b/services/core/Android.bp
index f8d19ec9..c5cfe921 100644
--- a/services/core/Android.bp
+++ b/services/core/Android.bp
@@ -186,6 +186,7 @@ java_library_static {
         "com.android.sysprop.watchdog",
         "ImmutabilityAnnotation",
         "securebox",
+        "rockchip.uhf.aidl-java", // AIDL, UHF-SRS-001 - see com.android.server.uhf.UhfHalTransport
     ],
     javac_shard_size: 50,
     javacflags: [
